Short Intro and About the Job :

Do you **love** **innovation****, project management, and the transformative power of AI?** Are you a analytical person armed with an open mind? Then apply now and join us as our **new operation project management intern in our Zoetermeer office** starting **May!**



In this internship, you will be part of the Medical NLD Ops team, within Operations category. Our purpose is to enhance productivity, efficiency and decision\-making through smart automation and data\-driven tools. Your main responsibilities include:

* Analyze current project management processes and tools to identify areas where AI can be integrated.
* Collaborate with stakeholders to collect and prepare relevant data for AI applications.
* Support the development and implementation of AI tools and insights to improve operations.
* Contribute to change management initiatives and training efforts related to AI integration.

**Meet your future manager!**



Your manager will be Kelly Veilbrief, Senior Operations Project Manager.


About You:

As an operation project management intern, it is a must that you have a strong affinity with AI. You have a problem\-solving mindset and data analytics ability. On top of that? You’re a communicative team worker who’s always looking for opportunities to learn and develop.

 **There are also some compulsory requirements:**

* Enrolled as a Bachelors/Masters student during the whole internship period;
* You are a resident of the Netherlands and hold a valid BSN number (if you are a non\-EU citizen, you need to have a valid Dutch residency permit);
* Ideally available to start in May for a minimum of 6 months, 4\-5 days per week;
* You are fluent in English \- spoken and written;
* You are able to work from our Zoetermeer office, at least 3 days per week.



About Us, We offer and What's next:

At Danone we are committed to our mission “bringing health, through food to as many people as possible”. Working together to make sure that our brands, like Hipro, Nutricia, Alpro, Activia, Nutrilon and Evian, create real benefits for people, communities and the planet. You will be part of one of the largest Certified B Corps™ in the world. Being B Corp means to be part of a select movement of companies verified to be meeting the highest standards of social and environmental criteria and using business as a force for good. One Planet. One Health.

 **We offer:**

* A competitive gross internship allowance of 650 euros per month (based on a full\-time internship);
* Home working allowance of 2\.45 euros per day;
* A public transport travel card covering all office\-related travel;
* Career advice opportunities such as workshops, seminars, networking events;
* International environment with 140 different nationalities in Danone NL;
* Active Internship community with 100\+ interns across the Netherlands.


